<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Desmond</h1><p class="st-meta">1118 CE – 1596 CE (approx.) · capital Cork; later Pallis</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The MacCarthy kingdom of South Munster, created when Munster was split in 1118 and surviving in parts until the end of the 16th century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-glanmire">Treaty of Glanmire</a> in 1118 divided <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-munster">Munster</a>, giving the south, Deasmumu, to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-maccarthy">MacCarthys</a>, heirs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eoganachta">Eoganacht</a> kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rock-of-cashel">Cashel</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cormac-mac-carthaigh">Cormac MacCarthy</a> ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cork">Cork</a> and built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cormacs-chapel">Cormac's Chapel</a> on the Rock of Cashel, consecrated in 1134.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Desmond's kings lost much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cork">Cork</a> to the Normans after 1177, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finghin-mac-carthaigh">Finghin MacCarthy</a>'s victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-callann">Callann</a> in 1261 halted the colonists. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-maccarthy">MacCarthy</a> Mor branch then ruled from Pallis in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ciarraige-luachra">Kerry</a>, with cadet lines in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carbery-county-cork">Carbery</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muskerry">Muskerry</a>. The kingdom was an overlordship of Gaelic lords such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osullivan-dynasty">O'Sullivans</a> and O'Donoghues.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donal-maccarthy-mor-1st-earl-of-clancare">Donal MacCarthy Mor</a> became Earl of Clancare in 1565 under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-ireland">Kingdom of Ireland</a>. His death without a legitimate male heir in 1596 ended the senior line, and its lands passed into English plantations.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-desmond.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Desmond" width="320" height="400"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was (Automated conversion) at English Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ireland_1450.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1118 CE – 1596 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cork; later Pallis</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Cormac MacCarthy, Finghin MacCarthy, Donal MacCarthy Mor</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Deasmumu, South Munster, MacCarthy Mor</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1357&amp;focus=kingdom-of-desmond" aria-label="Kingdom of Desmond on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4466 379 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Desmond lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4786 635L4823 622M4786 635L4861 599M4786 635L4861 599"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4823 622h0M4861 599h0M4861 599h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4786 635h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4786 635h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1357&amp;focus=kingdom-of-desmond">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
